roulette (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `roulette` is now a real roulette table: a single-zero wheel, the full
    betting layout (straights, splits, streets, corners, six lines, dozens,
    columns, even money) and an interactive table with re-bets and history.
  * Zero house edge: landing on 0 pays bets on 0 at 36:1 and sends every
    other bet to a SUPER SPIN on 1-36, so every bet has an EV of exactly 0.
  * The command wheel moved to --commands (and --russian). Red/black bets
    that land on a green "loser" command get a second-chance super spin.
  * --stats shows chips wagered, realized return and recent numbers.
  * A random fancy croupier (Gaston, Céleste, Lorenzo, ...): comments on bets and results, accepts tips
    (tip / --tip, no effect on the odds), and calls out the Martingale.
  * The ball occasionally escapes the wheel; straight-up hits get fireworks.
  * Break the Bank: runs start at 100 chips and are won at 1000. The croupier
    lasts the whole run; each chip tipped is +5% luck (max 30%) that a losing
    spin gets rigged your way, fading over 10 spins, until the pit boss
    catches you. Odds: 10% -> ~40% with steady tipping. Luck shows as 🍀 +5%;
    a 0 tip is -5%, and negative luck gets winning spins spoiled.
  * `swap_table` / --swap-table moves you to a table with a new croupier
    (luck resets; blocked for 5 spins after a bust). Seven more croupiers, 21 in all.
  * Each pit-boss bust doubles the catch chance for the rest of the run, at
    every table, so swapping tables can't dodge the consequences.

 -- Roulette Maintainer <sourcecodeholdings@protonmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

roulette (1.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added --beg: the only way to earn chips back. Beg while broke and the
    house spots you 100 (through 20 escalating levels of sass); beg with
    money and it mocks you. Tracks how many times you have gone broke.

 -- Roulette Maintainer <sourcecodeholdings@protonmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

roulette (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Super-random wildcard pockets: land on one and it runs a high-entropy
    command, turns the output into red/black, lights up the wheel and
    declares a winner (settles bets against the derived color).
  * Spinning wheel now alternates red/black instead of clumping colors.
  * Betting: show the win/lose verdict before running the command so its
    flavor output can't be mistaken for the result.

 -- Roulette Maintainer <sourcecodeholdings@protonmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

roulette (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cross-platform support (Linux + macOS) with per-OS command sets.
  * Added cheeky, harmless "losing" commands to the wheel.
  * Betting: colored red/black/green/jackpot pockets, a persistent bankroll,
    win streaks and a --stats view.
  * Removed snap packaging; install via .deb or from source.
  * Fixed a cal command that failed on hosts without cal.

